ask(c,'For column input x with shape3x1, what shapes make a1=ReLU(W1*x+b1) represent all four hidden neurons?', ['W1:4x3; b1:4x1; a1:4x1','W1:3x4; b1:3x1; a1:3x1','W1:4x4; b1:4x1; a1:4x1','W1:1x3; b1:1x1; a1:4x1'],['Matrix multiplication produces four preactivations, one per hidden neuron.','The weight matrix has the wrong orientation for a3x1 input.','Four columns cannot multiply the given3x1 vector.','A single row produces one scalar, not four outputs.'],kind='diagram',formula=[fm('a1=ReLU(W1*x+b1)',{'x':'3x1 input column','W1':'4x3 hidden-layer weights','b1':'4x1 bias column','a1':'4x1 hidden activation column'},{'all':'dimensionless'},['ReLU applied elementwise.'])],locator='Hidden-layer equation and node counts',conflict=(1038,'Vector layer equation is described as output of the first neuron.','Use a row of W1 and one bias component for a scalar neuron, or full matrix for the entire layer.'))
