ask(c,'A supplied regression task requires an unconstrained real-valued output. Which output activation avoids restricting predictions to a probability interval?', ['Identity/linear','Logistic sigmoid','Three-class softmax','Binary step'],['Identity preserves arbitrary real preactivations.','Sigmoid restricts the output to(0,1).','Softmax returns normalized nonnegative probabilities.','Step returns only0 or1.'],kind='scenario',assumptions=['Unbounded real target representation; this variant clarifies the output-format principle.'],pages=[1039,1049],locator='Output formatting and linear worked example')
