c=concept(1042,'Loss purpose and evaluation scope','Loss compares prediction and target; validation loss is possible without learning; common task families.')
ask(c,'Which match follows the lecture’s common loss choices?', ['Cross-entropy for classification probabilities; MSE for real-valued regression','Cross-entropy only for physical torque units; MSE only for class labels','MSE for layer counts; cross-entropy for sensor wiring','Cross-entropy for choosing the number of neurons; MSE for fixing output labels'],['These are common choices, not claims that every alternative loss is invalid.','The restrictions do not match the definitions.','Neither is a wiring or architecture-count metric.','Losses evaluate predictions rather than directly choose architecture or overwrite labels.'],kind='match',locator='Common loss list')
ask(c,'A model is frozen and evaluated on labeled validation examples. May its supervised loss be computed without updating weights?', ['Yes; computing evaluation loss does not itself train the model','No; any computed loss necessarily changes weights','No; labels may be used only during gradient updates','Yes, but only if the validation labels are first replaced by predictions'],['Loss can evaluate generalization with parameters held fixed, contradicting the source’s training-only wording.','Parameter updates require a separate operation.','Labeled held-out data can be used for evaluation.','Replacing targets would destroy the intended evaluation.'],kind='scenario',conflict=(1042,'Loss is used during training only.','A frozen model can compute loss on held-out labeled data without gradients or updates; the linked TensorFlow Playground itself displays test loss.'))
ask(c,'During ordinary inference with no known target, which part of the supervised cycle is still directly available?', ['A forward prediction, even when supervised target-dependent loss cannot be evaluated','A target-dependent loss that is guaranteed zero','A true-label gradient computed without any target or alternative objective','A proof of generalization from one prediction'],['The current model maps inputs to outputs without needing a true label.','Unknown targets do not imply zero error.','The specified supervised loss requires target information.','One prediction cannot establish generalization.'],kind='scenario',locator='Loss compares prediction to actual label')
