ask(c,'Training loss has stopped decreasing. What conclusion is justified without further checks?', ['The chosen stopping rule may trigger, but a global minimum or good held-out performance is not thereby proved','The model must have reached the unique global minimum','The model must predict every unseen example correctly','All gradients must be exactly zero even with finite precision and an excessive rate'],['Plateaus, numerical effects or poor step choices can stop observed decrease.','The stopping observation alone does not prove uniqueness or globality.','Training behavior does not guarantee generalization.','Oscillation or rounding can prevent decrease without zero gradients.'],locator='Iterate until loss stops decreasing',conflict=(1047,'Stopping when loss stops decreasing is called convergence without qualification.','Treat it as a practical rule, not a proof of optimality or generalization.'))
